`Glob::update` (defs.rs:2507-2511) converts the flag value to a string and pushes it onto `LowArgs.globs`:

```rust
fn update(&self, v: FlagValue, args: &mut LowArgs) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let glob = convert::string(v.unwrap_value())?;
    args.globs.push(glob);
    Ok(())
}
```

So each `-g`/`--glob` occurrence is converted to a `String` and appended to the `globs: Vec<String>` field of `LowArgs`.

`Glob::update` (crates/core/flags/defs.rs:2507-2511) converts the flag's value to a `String` and pushes it onto `args.globs` (a `Vec<String>` field on `LowArgs`):

```rust
fn update(&self, v: FlagValue, args: &mut LowArgs) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let glob = convert::string(v.unwrap_value())?;
    args.globs.push(glob);
    Ok(())
}
```

So each `-g`/`--glob` occurrence is appended to `LowArgs::globs`, rather than overwriting a single value — consistent with the flag's doc comment noting multiple `--glob` flags may be used.
